important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le17ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Be Supposed To"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + To be + supposed to + verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are not supposed to</span> come to dinner tonight.<br/> I <span class=\"strong\">am supposed to</span> give out Halloween candy.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "**Pronunciation tip**: When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am supposed to give out candy, then I am supposed to go to a costume party. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was supposed to go to a friend's house for dinner. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Later tonight, I am supposed to go dancing. <br/> <br/>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the first conditional with <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clauses to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes.<br/> You use the second conditional to exchange opinions about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the first conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not will or will not happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The parts of the sentence are divided into two clauses: the <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause and the <span class=\"italic\">condition</span> clause.<span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the second conditional to talk about hypothetical situations. There is no certainty that it's possible to fulfill the condition. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I  had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/> What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past verb</span> + <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">would</span></span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional: 2nd Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I study today, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll go to the party tonight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that I can go to the party tonight, but only if I study first. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I were a child again, I would freak out!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I would be putting on my elegant costume if I were a little girl."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I were a child at Halloween again, I would be a princess."}, {"type": "text", "content": " "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional:<br/>If ... + Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional: would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If I were a child again,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I would be a princess for Halloween.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is an impossible situation because you are not a child  and thus, this can only happen in a hypothetical situation.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to freak out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to be in a heightened emotional state such as fear or excitement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I were a child again, I would freak out!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are the words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "elegant "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "tasteful or refined"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would be putting on my elegant costume if I were a little girl getting ready to go out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sacred "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dedicated or in relation to a deity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Superstitions are magical and sometimes sacred. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fan"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone that is devoted to or admires something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope to hear from all my fans again for the next mailbag bunch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bunch "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a group of things that are related with each other and gathered in the same place."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope to hear from all my fans again for the next mailbag bunch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to address "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to direct the attention towards something specific"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All of your superstition emails were read, but if I didn't address yours, I am sorry."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "curse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a source or cause of evil"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A lot of you wrote about superstitions and the curse of bad luck. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "victim "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone that gets harmed or killed by someone else"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I were you I wouldn't worry about being lucky. Don't be a victim. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob11aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Share a few unusual superstitions with the class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask them if they think these superstitions are true or untrue. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make sure you encourage your students to share the reasons behind their responses. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Reveal that a few of your superstitions are false."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In pairs, have students write four superstitions and the description of the superstition. The superstition can be true or it can be false."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Separate the pairs and put them in small groups."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A person reads a superstition and the group members must guess if it's true or false and explain why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Continue to the next person."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about superstitions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about things I am/was supposed to do and things that are/were supposed to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present information clearly and confidently."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen for gist and details."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about manners, customs and superstitions. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about things I am/was supposed to do and                           things that are/were supposed to happen."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Who is the luckiest person you know? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Why is that person lucky?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Are you a lucky person? Why or why not?"}], 